  b.stage('armor-local-api','Provide armor support through local workstation IPC','cryptoComputer','cryptoClient','Alice’s Kerberos exchange obtains the selected computer armor result locally.','The shared workstation’s protected credential API supplies opaque AP-REQ and derived armor_key to the selected local user exchange. This explicit local IPC is not a KDC packet; computer password and computer TGT session key remain in the computer context.',b.wire([f.ArmorApReq,f.ArmorKey],'cryptoComputer','cryptoClient','Supplies the armor AP-REQ and derived armor key through local protected IPC.','local workstation credential API'),[b.p(f.ArmorApReq)],[b.put('keys.armorClient',{instanceId:b.refs[f.ArmorKey].instanceId,source:'computer credential context'})],[], 'local-ipc');
  b.stage('user-challenge','Create Alice’s protected password challenge','cryptoClient','cryptoClient','The computer armor protects transport; Alice still proves her own credential.','Derive clientchallengearmor/challengelongterm with Alice’s long-term key, then encrypt PA-ENC-TS-ENC with usage 54. The padata type is PA-ENCRYPTED-CHALLENGE (138), not PA-ENC-TIMESTAMP (2).',[...b.op([f.ArmorKey,f.LongTermKey],'use','cryptoClient','Uses the distinct armor and user long-term keys.'),...b.op([f.ClientChallengeKey,f.Challenge],'derive','cryptoClient','Derives the client-direction challenge key and encrypts the freshness structure.')],[b.p(f.Challenge)],[b.put('keys.clientChallenge',{instanceId:b.refs[f.ClientChallengeKey].instanceId,usage:54})]);
  b.stage('protect-request','Bind the outer body and encrypt the FAST inner request','cryptoClient','cryptoClient','The workstation creates a protected envelope containing Alice’s real request.','req-checksum uses armor_key and usage 50 over the exact outer KDC-REQ-BODY. enc-fast-req uses usage 51 over DER KrbFastReq{fast-options,padata,req-body}. The protected inner body is separate from outer metadata.',[...b.op([f.OuterBody,f.InnerBody,f.FastOptions,f.Nonce,f.Armor],'create','cryptoClient','Creates separate outer and inner request objects.'),...b.op([f.ArmorKey,f.Challenge,f.Usage50,f.Usage51],'use','cryptoClient','Uses armor and the selected challenge with distinct cryptographic usages.'),...b.op([f.ReqChecksum,f.EncReq,f.FastRequest],'derive','cryptoClient','Computes the bound checksum and encrypted FAST request.')],[b.p(f.ReqChecksum),b.p(f.EncReq)],[b.put('keys.fastRequest',{instanceId:b.refs[f.EncReq].instanceId,usage:51})]);
  b.stage('fast-request','Send armored user AS-REQ','cryptoClient','cryptoKdc','The KDC receives explicit computer armor and the encrypted user request.','The wire packet has outer request metadata, armor AP-REQ, req-checksum and enc-fast-req. Inner user challenge/body are ciphertext contents; keys and decoded inner fields are not exposed wire parameters.',b.wire([f.OuterBody,f.FastRequest,f.Armor,f.ArmorApReq,f.ReqChecksum,f.EncReq],'cryptoClient','cryptoKdc','Carries the explicit AS armor and encrypted FAST container.','AS-REQ / PA-FX-FAST'),[b.p(f.OuterBody),b.p(f.Armor),b.p(f.ReqChecksum),b.p(f.EncReq)]);
  b.stage('armor-kdc','Validate computer armor and derive the KDC armor key','cryptoKdc','cryptoKdc','The KDC authenticates the armor credential independently of Alice’s credential.','Decrypt/validate the computer TGT and its fresh authenticator, recover mandatory subkey, then apply CF2(subkey,ticket_session_key,"subkeyarmor","ticketarmor"). The derived armor key stays local.',[...b.op([f.Armor,f.ArmorApReq,f.ArmorTicket,f.Subkey,f.ArmorTicketKey],'verify','cryptoKdc','Validates the computer armor AP-REQ and recovers its inputs locally.'),...b.op([f.ArmorKey],'derive','cryptoKdc','Derives the same conversation armor key.')],[],[b.put('keys.armorKdc',{instanceId:b.refs[f.ArmorKey].instanceId}),b.put('checks.computerArmor',true)]);
  b.stage('request-binding','Check the bound request'+(variant==='checksum'?'':' and decode the inner body'),'cryptoKdc','cryptoKdc','The KDC checks that the protected request belongs to this outer request.',variant==='checksum'?'The usage-50 checksum does not bind these exact outer-body bytes. Stop before interpreting the inner request.':'Validate req-checksum over the outer AS body with usage 50, then decrypt enc-fast-req with usage 51. Only the KDC’s successful local decode exposes the inner request and challenge.',[...b.op([f.ReqChecksum,f.OuterBody,f.Usage50],'verify','cryptoKdc','Checks the exact AS outer-body checksum.'),...(variant==='checksum'?[]:[...b.op([f.EncReq,f.ArmorKey,f.Usage51],'use','cryptoKdc','Decrypts the FAST request only after valid armor/binding.'),...b.op([f.InnerBody,f.FastOptions,f.Nonce],'verify','cryptoKdc','Processes the decoded inner request body and options.')])],[],[b.put('checks.fastRequestBinding',variant!=='checksum')]);
